{
  "requirement": "The `mdbook` subcommand MUST act as the mdBook preprocessor for HTML books, rendering requirement definitions and linked reference badges. This project's `book.toml` MUST configure `cargo habeas mdbook` as the `habeas` preprocessor, using a repository-local Cargo alias for `cargo run --release -p habeas --`. Consumer books MUST continue to invoke the installed `habeas mdbook` CLI directly.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has three obligations, and the reviewed tests cover each one.\n\n1. **The `mdbook` subcommand acts as the preprocessor for HTML books.** It renders requirement definitions and linked reference badges.\n   - `tests/repository.rs#fn[mdbook_preprocessor_renders_definitions_between_stdin_and_stdout]` spawns the real `habeas mdbook` binary. It sends a serialized `(PreprocessorContext, Book)` for renderer `html` on stdin and parses the `Book` from stdout.\n   - It asserts that the `:::{req}` directives are gone from the output.\n   - It asserts that two definition badge rows are rendered, and that each has kind and name badge links, no inline `<svg>`, and two `</a>` links.\n   - It asserts that a `{cite}` reference to `rules.ready` is rendered as a Shields badge (`https://img.shields.io/badge/`). The badge links to `#habeas-req-rules.ready` and to `requirements-index/rules.ready.html`.\n   - It also checks the generated index chapter and its detail pages.\n   - The assertions would catch a no-op preprocessor, a missing badge or a missing link.\n2. **This project's `book.toml` configures `cargo habeas mdbook` as the `habeas` preprocessor, through a repository-local alias for `cargo run --release -p habeas --`.**\n   - `tests/repository.rs#fn[project_book_uses_the_repository_local_preprocessor_alias]` parses the repository's `book.toml`. It asserts `preprocessor.habeas.command == \"cargo habeas mdbook\"` and the `renderers` setting.\n   - It parses `.cargo/config.toml` and asserts `alias.habeas == \"run --release -p habeas --\"`.\n3. **Consumer books continue to invoke the installed `habeas mdbook` CLI directly.**\n   - `tests/setup.rs#fn[setup_is_repeatable]` runs setup twice. It asserts the generated `book.toml` contains `command = \"habeas mdbook\"`, which is the direct invocation and not the cargo alias.\n\nI found no untested obligation and no wrong expected result. The text does not specify non-HTML renderers, so they need no test.",
